  "full_text": "So, Jesus killed the swine. He caused a herd of 2,000 swine to go kill themselves. Something like that. So, legion, you know. Anyway, so, you know, what's his name? J.R.R. Tolkien. Talk of orcs and goblins and stuff. I think that was straight out of World War I. world war one um so uh what is a hacker um you know uh uh sometimes this is kind of interesting uh as kind of a personal uh guilt complex my handwriting is kind of bad and uh sometimes i i i do brutal uh on a computer it'll uh it'll accept uh abbreviated uh entries into a search engine and stuff like that And, you know, maybe you begin to look like a hacker or something like that. I don't know. Like Bill Gates started using the word for programmers or something. I didn't like it because I thought it was like a bad surgeon butcher or something, you know. And I was like, oh, I don't want to be a hacker. Anyway, it's kind of interesting to look at it from... You know, there's like legitimate, legit in the ghetto or something, I guess. And then there's like, like maybe a hacker. You ever seen like the really carefully crafted penmanship and stuff? That's kind of the, you know, Catholics are always looking to give themselves guilt. And so sometimes I meditate on, well, once in a while, I meditate on, oh no, I'm not. I'm in too much of a hurry and it's kind of ugly like a like a orc or something, you know, so I don't know",
